"""Generate review evidence only; not a source-question generator."""
import importlib.util,json
from pathlib import Path
D=Path(__file__).parent
spec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('g',D.with_suffix('.py'));g=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec);spec.loader.exec_module(g)
s=json.loads((D/'source.json').read_text());cases=json.loads((D/'source-cases.json').read_text())
records=[];review=['# Identifying Singular Matrices: review\n','Database math, basis 1356, lineage '+s['lineage']+'. These are local review records; no registration or writes. Originals are shown verbatim. Generated arithmetic uses exact equivalent formatting and the same number of solution stages. Choice-bank whitespace is preserved.\n']
for case in cases:
 q=next(q for q in s['record'][':knowledge-point/questions']if q[':question/math-academy-id']==case['source_id']);f=q[':question/answer-fields'][case['source_field_index']]
 review+=['## Original '+case['source_id']+' / field '+str(case['source_field_index'])+'\n',q[':question/problem']+'\n','\n'.join('- '+a[':answer/value']for a in f[':answer-field/choices'])+'\n','Original correct designation: '+str(case['correct_original'])+'\n',q[':question/worked-solution']+'\n']
 r=g.generate(case['level'],template=case['template'],parameters=case['parameters'],profile=case['bank_profile']);records.append({'role':'source-replay','source_id':case['source_id'],'source_field_index':case['source_field_index'],'record':r})
 review+=['### Parameterized original replay\n',g.markdown(r)+'\n']
 for seed in (13,41):
  r=g.generate(case['level'],seed=seed,template=case['template'],profile=case['bank_profile']);records.append({'role':'generated-variant','source_id':case['source_id'],'record':r})
  review+=['### Generated variant ('+case['level']+', seed '+str(seed)+', '+case['template']+', '+case['bank_profile']+')\n',g.markdown(r)+'\n']
for seed in (13,41):
 r=g.generate_hard(seed);records.append({'role':'authored-hard','record':r});review+=['## Authored hard example / seed '+str(seed)+'\n',g.markdown(r)+'\n']
(D/'review.md').write_text('\n'.join(review));(D/'review.json').write_text(json.dumps(records,indent=2))
classify=['# Classification\n','Snapshot: math / basis 1356 / lineage '+s['lineage']+'. Captured source.json is unchanged.\n','| Level | Practices | Observed Markdown/value templates | Field | Plot rating |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|']
for level in ('easy','moderate','hard'):
 qs=[q for q in s['record'][':knowledge-point/questions']if q[':question/difficulty'][':db/ident'].endswith('/'+level)]
 ts=[t for t,v in g.TEMPLATES.items()if v['level']==level and v['source_ids']]
 classify.append(f'| {level} | {len(qs)} | {len(ts)} | One five-choice text radio, key selection | none |')
classify+=['\nThere are 15 observed structural templates, 8 complete bank profiles, and 18 raw fields across 17 questions. Templates distinguish statement order/type, bullet/roman/roman-spaced layout, difficulty, and the compact five-stage versus full six-stage solution. Changed matrix values are variants, not separate templates. Easy bullet det/singular/det and moderate bullet singular/det/det each combine two sources.\n','Hard has one authored template, not an observed level label. It keeps the same three-statement radio task and top-row cofactor method. Dense nonzero entries use signed fractions and one repeated radical family: fraction minors are present in q-77478 and q-38187, fraction/radical cancellation in q-128490, and squared radicals in q-128491. The repeated radical follows those existing arithmetic operations, without introducing a new radical-combination branch. Easy uses small signed integers; moderate uses fraction columns, radical columns, or a combination as in the originals. Each level samples singular/nonsingular matrices without a progression.\n','The lesson route (followed via first-step and next) is Introduction → Calculating the Determinant → Singular Matrices → Identifying Singular Matrices → Solving for a Variable → Solving for an Unknown. This KP stops at numeric determinant and singularity. The key prerequisite is Introduction to the Inverse of a Matrix; the singular tutorial defines det=0 and no multiplicative inverse. Unknown entries, inverses, and row reduction are excluded.\n','## Source-format anomaly\n','q-128490 contains two raw selection fields; legacy field 3834be7c-3d92-5a42-ba11-b5873d0a2001 has no correct reference. The captured original MA lesson widget (q-128490-authoritative-widget.json and /home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/153/Source/Sections/08-question-128490.png, inspected) contains one five-choice bank. Both raw fields have the identical complete value set, with the newer field carrying correct III only. Exact expansion derives 0. Normal generation produces one assessment; source replay profiles retain both field banks. The missing legacy designation is inferred, never counted as matched. The newer raw field resolves the assessment; no source is excluded.\n','q-77477 and q-128491 have malformed bold **not ** in their closing sentence; generated prose repairs **not**. q-77477 answer whitespace (I  only / I and III  only) remains exactly captured. Mathematical typography, whitespace, coefficient sign/parentheses, and commuted products are normalized, separately from bank fidelity. All arithmetic rows are independently verified as exact equalities.\n','## Templates\n','| Template | Sources | Stages |\n|---|---|---:|']
for t,v in g.TEMPLATES.items():classify.append(f"| {t} | {', '.join(v['source_ids']) or 'authored'} | {v['solution_rows']} |")
(D/'classification.md').write_text('\n'.join(classify))
extraction=['# Template extraction\n','All four stages use the unchanged basis-1356 capture. No original content is read by the runtime generator. recipes.json stores structure and complete categorical profiles; source-cases.json stores only explicit input values for normal replay.\n','## 1. Describe each original before generalizing\n']
for q in s['record'][':knowledge-point/questions']:
 cs=[c for c in cases if c['source_id']==q[':question/math-academy-id']];c=cs[0];t=g.TEMPLATES[c['template']]
 extraction += ['### '+c['source_id']+'\n','Level: '+c['level']+'. Matrix '+c['parameters']['name']+' entries by rows: `'+json.dumps(c['parameters']['matrix'])+'`.\n','Statement kinds in order: '+', '.join(t['statements'])+'; claims: `'+json.dumps(c['parameters']['claims'])+'`. Layout '+t['layout']+'; solution '+str(t['solution_rows'])+' stages. All values are finite exact real constants; no variable is solved. '+('Radicals/fractions occur.'if any('/'in v or 'sqrt'in v for v in c['parameters']['matrix'])else'Signed integers only.')+'\n','Profiles: '+', '.join(c['bank_profile']for c in cs)+'. Raw field count '+str(len(cs))+'.\n']
extraction+=['## 2. Shared mathematical pattern\n','Expand the numeric 3×3 determinant across the first row, evaluate three 2×2 minors, simplify signed products, compare the determinant with zero, and choose the exact subset of true I/II/III statements. The compact q-77477 pattern combines the evaluated-terms stage with the final simplification. Statements may be numeric determinant equalities, singular, or nonsingular. The matrices are named, and names have no mathematical role.\n','## 3. Components and complete-bank mapping\n','Each matrix entry a..i is an explicit parameter. Three claims are explicit prompt parameters only at determinant-statement positions; other positions are null. Correct set is computed independently from det=a(ei−fh)−b(di−fg)+c(dh−eg). The answer fragments are fixed categorical subsets, not fitted numerical distractors. A source choice saying I and III only represents exactly truth subset {1,3}; its error interpretation is deliberately not guessed. Each source choice is mapped below, preserving its exact value/whitespace and original field assignment. All five choices form a single eligible profile; it is selected before parameter sampling and rejected as a whole if the mathematically correct subset is absent.\n']
for name,bank in g.BANK_PROFILES.items():
 extraction+=['### '+name+'\n','Original fields: '+', '.join(sid+' / '+str(i)for sid,i in bank['source_fields'])+'.\n','| Exact source fragment | Recipe (statement-index subset) | Replay |\n|---|---|---|']
 for v in bank['values']:extraction.append('| `'+v+'` | '+str(g.subset(v))+' | exact complete text match |')
 extraction+=['']
extraction+=['## 4. Reusable Markdown/value template\n','Fixed prompt: “Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $NAME$ given below?” Three ordered statements use the observed bullet/roman layout followed by NAME=[matrix] in display math. Fixed solution opening and cofactor explanation follow the captured sentences. Variable components: all nine exact entries, three determinant claims at applicable positions, matrix name, evaluated minors/products/determinant, truth conclusion. Source formatting style retains optional ne0, trailing explanation spaces, and blank line before Since. Malformed bold is repaired. No distractor-specific feedback is added.\n','Full solution stages: determinant matrix → first-row minor expansion → evaluated pair-products in minor parentheses → evaluated minors → evaluated signed terms → determinant. Compact stages preserve the same first three stages, combine unit-coefficient pair products with evaluated nonunit-coefficient minors, then determinant. Parentheses, explicit multiplication, product order, and zero terms are canonically rendered; the same stage count and every complete equality are replay-checked, not asserted byte-identical.\n','Constraints: nine real finite exact algebraic constants, exactly three claims matching statement kinds, one capital name, distinct determinant claims, and a complete five-choice bank with one unique correct truth subset. Explicit invalid input fails; sampled invalid input rejects the whole instance. No floats, symbols, nonreal radicals, infinity, duplicate semantic options, or missing choices. Identity covers learner prompt/solution and the complete displayed bank; seed and shuffling are excluded. Mathematical fingerprint excludes matrix name and bank.\n','Sampling bounds (authored policies): easy/moderate base entries −5..8 (covering all observed integer entries), hard base entries −4..4 to control exact arithmetic, singular third row u*r1+v*r2 for (u,v) in {(1,1),(2,−1),(−1,2),(1,−2)}, or independent nonsingular rows. Easy keeps integers. Moderate applies one fraction column 1/d, d∈{2,3,5,7}, one radical column sqrt(q), q∈{2,3,5,7}, or both in different columns. These observed number types can coexist as in q-128490/q-128484. Source matrices with mixed kinds within a column remain supported by explicit replay; column scaling is a documented narrower sampling policy, not a claim that all observed structures arose from it. Hard requires all nine entries nonzero and applies sqrt(q)/d, 1/e, sqrt(q)/f to three columns (d∈{2,3,4,5}, e∈{2,3,5}, f∈{2,3,4}). This repeats a supported radical family and keeps exact products within source fraction/radical arithmetic. Both determinant-zero/nonzero states are sampled; numeric claims choose exact det or independent small integers −10..10, 0, ±1. Default easy/moderate banks are selected from the profiles actually observed for that template. Hard and explicitly requested cross-template banks reuse an entire observed categorical bank and label it authored-reuse/profile_extension; no option is mixed into another bank.\n','Generalization limits: observed categorical bank fragments are exact. Original distractor-making intent is not recoverable and is not claimed. The source mathematics has no detected errors. The duplicate field, missing legacy correct ref, and malformed bold are documented in classification and counted separately in validation. Hard is authored because no source difficulty label supports it. The density policy is a scoped design claim, anchored to named moderate originals and the lesson definition.\n']
(D/'template-extraction.md').write_text('\n'.join(extraction))
(D/'plot-extraction.md').write_text('# Plot extraction / specification\n\nPlot rating: none for all observed and authored templates. The canonical example image 21cd71e00c682ad1117b9ae126adcbeb8e4c55769c73eae1e1169534f2a01d4a.png was inspected: it is only the numeric 3×3 matrix [[1,2,3],[1,0,1],[3,4,7]]. Mathematical typography is not a plot. All practice prompts embed their matrices in LaTeX. No parameter-dependent graphical asset, renderer, or plot generation is required for steps 5 and 7.\n')
(D/'README.md').write_text('''# Identifying Singular Matrices (17592186059848)

Numeric 3×3 determinant calculation followed by a three-statement singularity classification. All three levels are implemented. Hard is an authored density/fraction/repeated-radical policy anchored to the observed moderate examples. No other matrix skill, database transaction, or plot is included.

Run from the repository root:

```sh
.venv/bin/python generate/scratch/17592186059848.py --difficulty all --seed 13 --count 2
.venv/bin/python generate/scratch/17592186059848/validate.py
.venv/bin/python generate/scratch/17592186059848/write_review.py
```

The public functions are generate_easy, generate_moderate, generate_hard, and generate(level, seed=0, template=None, field_type=None, parameters=None, profile=None). Source replay uses source-cases.json through this same interface. Explicit invalid input fails. CLI supports --difficulty easy|moderate|hard|all, --seed, --count, --format markdown|json, --template and --profile.

source.json preserves math basis 1356 and lineage. recipes.json contains the extracted structure; build_evidence.py reproduces this read-only extraction from the fixed captures. review.md displays originals, parameterized replays, two generated variants per source field, and two authored hard examples; review.json holds the records. validation.json separates source banks/designations, independently parsed exact math, and actual native grading. engine-input.json and engine-report.json are memory-only native grader fixtures and results.

q-128490 has two identical raw banks at a duplicate field key and one missing legacy correct reference. The captured widget proves one five-choice assessment; normal generation emits one field. Both raw banks are replayed, but the missing original correct designation is reported as inferred, not matched. Arithmetic typography and malformed source bold are normalized and documented separately from complete bank matches.
''')
